.TH trellis-version-apply 1 "" trellis "Trellis Manual"
.SH NAME
trellis\-version\-apply \- Bump versions, render changelogs, patch manifest.toml locked versions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrellis version apply\fR [\fB\-\-bump\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-set\fR] [\fB\-\-pre\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bump versions, render changelogs, patch manifest.toml locked versions
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bump\fR \fI<LEVEL|PKG=LEVEL>\fR
Override the derived bump level, workspace\-wide (`\-\-bump major`) or for one package (`\-\-bump lat_core=major`). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Run as if started in this directory
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
When to color output. `auto` follows the terminal, `NO_COLOR`, and `CLICOLOR=0`; the other two override that detection
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fI<PKG=VERSION>\fR
Pin a package\*(Aqs next version exactly (`\-\-set lat_core=1.0.0`). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-pre\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
Cut a prerelease: `\-\-pre rc` gives 1.0.0\-rc.1, and again 1.0.0\-rc.2. Fragments stay unreleased until the final version. `\-\-pre none` promotes the current prerelease to its final version and consumes them
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress normal\-path output; JSON/report payloads and errors still print
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit JSON listing every bump and patched lockfile
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Trace every command trellis shells out to, on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR
Don\*(Aqt check whether a newer trellis release is available

The check is also skipped in CI, when not attached to a terminal, and when `TRELLIS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK` or `DO_NOT_TRACK` is set.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
